import MatedCRT.Defs.Setting

/-!
# Frozen external inputs of the measurable floor obstacle

Statements of external facts used in the measurable floor-obstacle development. Each is a `Prop`-valued `def`, consumed as an explicit hypothesis. Nothing here is proved in this repository.
-/

namespace MatedCRT

open MeasureTheory HarmonicBalls

/-- Least-supersolution membership for the LQG measure of a mated-CRT environment: almost surely, for every radius `ρ ∈ (0,1)` and every `t > 0`, the continuum least supersolution `leastSupersolution (S.μ ω) ρ 0 t` (pole `0`) belongs to `supersolutions (S.μ ω) ρ 0 t`, i.e. it is continuous on `B̄_ρ`, satisfies `Δw ≤ μ` on `B_ρ` (`LaplacianLE`) and lies above the obstacle `-t G_{B_ρ}(0,·)` off the pole. Source: Bou-Rabee and Gwynne, "Harmonic balls in Liouville quantum gravity", arXiv:2208.11795, Lemma 3.1 (`lemma:basic-properties`, printed line 621), in the form `LeastSupersolutionMemStmt` (Harmonic-Balls-LQG `HarmonicBalls/Draft/Section3.lean`), applied to the `γ`-LQG measure `S.μ` of the quantum cone `S.hC`, `S.hcirc` (`IsQuantumCone`, `IsLQGMeasure`, `Setting.lean`). The printed statement is for the LQG measure of a whole-plane GFF; the transfer from the quantum cone to that setting is checked below.
Truth check: TRUE. The cone is compared with a whole-plane GFF with insertion parameter `α₀ = γ`: IDLA, arXiv:2211.04891v2, (2.4), (2.8) and Fact 2.2(II), p. 12, give the restricted-field law and the measure locality; HB, arXiv:2208.11795v3, Lemma 3.1, p. 13, applied with `α₀ = γ`; its deterministic underpinning is HB Appendix A, pp. 65-67, especially Lemma A.1 (simultaneous parameters). -/
def FrozenLeastSupersolutionMemCone (𝒮 : SpaceFillingSLEModel) : Prop :=
  ∀ γ : ℝ, 0 < γ → γ < 2 → ∀ (Ω : Type) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (S : MatedCRTEnv Ω), S.IsValid 𝒮 γ →
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂S.P, ∀ ρ : ℝ, 0 < ρ → ρ < 1 → ∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t →
      leastSupersolution (S.μ ω) ρ 0 t ∈ supersolutions (S.μ ω) ρ 0 t

/-- Standard Borel structure of the finite measures on a closed disk: for every `ρ > 0`, the subtype `{ν : Measure ℂ | IsFiniteMeasure ν ∧ ν|_{B̄_ρ} = ν}` of Mathlib's measures (σ-algebra generated by the evaluations `ν ↦ ν(A)`) is a standard Borel space. Equivalently, the finite measures on the compact metric space `B̄_ρ` with the weak topology form a Polish space whose Borel σ-algebra is the evaluation σ-algebra. Source: standard measure theory (Kechris, Classical Descriptive Set Theory, Thm 17.23-17.24 and §17.E; Parthasarathy, Probability Measures on Metric Spaces, Thm II.6.2).
Truth check: TRUE. Kechris, *Classical Descriptive Set Theory* (1995), §17.E, Theorem 17.23, p. 112; Theorem 17.24, pp. 112-113; and the following paragraph, p. 113, followed by the finite-measure normalization (an isolated extra point).
Discharged: `MatedCRT.frozenFiniteMeasureDiskStandardBorel_holds` (`MatedCRT/FirstPass/LPBridge/FiniteMeasureStandardBorel.lean:18`) proves it. -/
def FrozenFiniteMeasureDiskStandardBorel : Prop :=
  ∀ ρ : ℝ, 0 < ρ →
    StandardBorelSpace {ν : Measure ℂ // IsFiniteMeasure ν ∧ ν.restrict (Metric.closedBall (0 : ℂ) ρ) = ν}

end MatedCRT
